## LLM PROVIDER — CLOUD ONLY (CRITICAL CONSTRAINT)
# This project uses CLOUD LLM APIs only. The developer's laptop cannot run local models.
# NEVER generate code that uses or references:
#   - Ollama (not installed, not available)
#   - llama.cpp (not installed)
#   - LocalAI (not installed)
#   - Any model running on localhost (except cloud APIs)
#   - ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (paid service — not configured)
#   - OPENAI_API_KEY (paid service — not configured)


# APPROVED CLOUD PROVIDERS (all free tier):
#   PRIMARY:   Groq        — console.groq.com     — gsk_ key prefix
#   FALLBACK:  Gemini      — aistudio.google.com  — AIzaSy key prefix
#   TERTIARY:  OpenRouter  — openrouter.ai        — sk-or-v1- key prefix


# CORRECT pattern for any LLM call in this project:
#   provider = LLMProvider()            # reads settings automatically
#   response = await provider.chat(...) # cloud call, auto-fallback


# WRONG patterns (never generate these):
#   import ollama                        # NOT ALLOWED
#   AsyncOllama(host="localhost:11434")  # NOT ALLOWED
#   httpx.post("http://localhost:...")   # NOT ALLOWED for LLM calls
#   from anthropic import AsyncAnthropic # NOT ALLOWED (paid)
#   openai.Client(...)                   # NOT ALLOWED (paid)


## WHEN GENERATING LLM CODE:
# Always use: from backend.app.services.llm_provider import LLMProvider
# Never import groq, genai, or httpx directly in business logic files
# Never hardcode model names — always read from settings.*_MODEL
